From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:20:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: asahi: enable ACPI for the CLPC's
 platform profiles

The CLPC offers macOS's power modes as platform profiles (T6050, T6041),
and APPLE_CLPC selects ACPI_PLATFORM_PROFILE only if ACPI: the
platform_profile class lives in drivers/acpi/ and is built only with
CONFIG_ACPI. The shared fragment does not set it, and with the
omarchy-pkgs linux-aurora base config ("# CONFIG_ACPI is not set") no
CLPC profile registers, so power-profiles-daemon falls back to its
placeholder platform driver.

Enable ACPI in the fragment. A device tree boot keeps ACPI disabled at
run time, and the platform_profile class registers without ACPI
firmware since "ACPI: platform_profile: Register the class without ACPI
firmware".

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config b/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config
index 31122c6ebf..8af592b1fb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config
@@ -16,6 +16,9 @@ CONFIG_ARM64_MEMORY_MODEL_CONTROL=y
 CONFIG_PAGE_BLOCK_MAX_ORDER=7
 CONFIG_ARM_APPLE_CPUIDLE=y
 CONFIG_ARM_APPLE_SOC_CPUFREQ=m
+# The CLPC's power modes are platform profiles, and the platform_profile
+# class builds only with ACPI. A device tree boot leaves ACPI disabled.
+CONFIG_ACPI=y
 CONFIG_THERMAL_GOV_POWER_ALLOCATOR=y
 # CONFIG_THERMAL_DEFAULT_GOV_STEP_WISE is not set
 CONFIG_THERMAL_DEFAULT_GOV_POWER_ALLOCATOR=y
-- 
2.43.0

